{"name":"Armour","hex":"#74857f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Armour","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A small city, the county seat of Douglas County, South Dakota, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Armour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Armour","blocks":[{"text":"Armour or armor is a covering used to protect an object, individual, or vehicle from physical injury or damage, especially direct contact weapons or projectiles during combat, or from a potentially dangerous environment or activity. Personal armour is used to protect soldiers and war animals. Vehicle armour is used on warships, armoured fighting vehicles, and some combat aircraft, mostly ground attack aircraft."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Xixia_Chainmail_Armor_%2841985701161%29.jpg/330px-Xixia_Chainmail_Armor_%2841985701161%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armour","wikidata":"Q11886611"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Arms_and_Armor_2010-09-18.jpg/500px-Arms_and_Armor_2010-09-18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Arms_and_Armor_2010-09-18.jpg/1280px-Arms_and_Armor_2010-09-18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Arms_and_Armor_2010-09-18.jpg/500px-Arms_and_Armor_2010-09-18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Armour “harness”. German, about AD 1540-50. Metropolitan Museum of At","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArms_and_Armor_2010-09-18.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Paris_bordone_016.jpg/500px-Paris_bordone_016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pa